{
    "background_story": "Edgar was a reclusive alchemist who spent most of his life studying the ancient arts of botany and mysticism. His obsession was the mythical Mandragora, a root said to hold the secrets of life and death. Legend had it that the Mandragora could only be harvested under the light of the full moon, and its screams could drive men mad. Undeterred, Edgar spent years searching for the elusive plant, pouring over dusty tomes and seeking out whispers of its whereabouts. Finally, after a decade of searching, he found it - a twisted, glowing root deep in the heart of the forest. As he reached for it, Edgar felt an otherworldly energy coursing through his veins, and he knew that his life's work was about to change forever. The Mandragora's power was said to be boundless, and Edgar was determined to unlock its secrets.",
